 of Queens and a Jack kicker (mediocre strength), betting would primarily get called by better hands (better kickers with Queens, trips, two pair, or straights) and fold worse hands. The opponent's passivity is suspicious - they could have a better Queen, or even trips/two pair. Checking is the prudent play to minimize losses while still having a chance to win at showdown if they're equally weak or bluffing.\n\n**Answer:** 0"}
